A||||6||BENGAL4||APPLYING RTV TO WATER PUMP
Z||000000||BENGAL4||07-27-99||07:35 PM||||When replacing the waterpump, I know you use RTV sealant along with the gasket. My question is, do you apply to one or two sides of the gasket. Someone, please respond quickly as I am in the middle of the job and the sealant is getting hard.<p><br>Bill
Z||000001||batboy||07-27-99||07:42 PM||||For the best sealing, apply a little to both sides. I have put water pumps on a number of times without any sealer with no problems, but a THIN coat is nice insurance, although makes it a little tougher to remove and clean up later on. Don't put too much on, you don't want any excess squeezed into the coolant passages, radiator, or into the inside of the water pump.
Z||000002||theogre||07-27-99||07:50 PM||||it should be applied Thinly to both sides. tho I expect I'm too late this time......<p>Personally I prefer "Aviation", Hi Tack, or Supper 300, sealers. These paint on/spray on sealers are much better on good surfaces. I only use RTV in things that are scratched up bad, or uneven like valve covers often are, and even then I'm real carefull how much I use. If you aren't carefull with RTV, pieces of sealant break off inside the motor and plug up a lifter of something. (I never use "Indian Head" shelack unless an application specifically calls for it like some classic resto work does.)
Z||000003||BENGAL4||07-27-99||07:53 PM||||Thanks, Batboy. 7 minutes for an answer. Thats great response time. Are you always on your computer? I have to split time with my girls (9 & 11) so when I get time, it's precious.<p><br>Bill
Z||000004||batboy||07-27-99||08:50 PM||||No life, wife (anymore), or kids so I can play on the computer all I want...too hot to work on my cars right now anyway.
Z||000005||BENGAL4||07-27-99||09:26 PM||||Never too hot to work on my car. The temp has been over 90 degrees the past twelve days. When you have a house full of women, the garage is the only place in my house that is mine and mine alone. Shoot, even my cats are female. But I wouldn,t have it any other way. In case your wondering, BENGAL4 is the plate number on my 86GT. Guess you can figure out what football team I root for.<p><br>Bill
